    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"dimension\",\n  \"unit\": null,\n  \"additive_over_entities\": null,\n  \"additive_over_time\": null,\n  \"time_rollup\": null,\n  \"valid_methods\": [],\n  \"period_basis\": null,\n  \"derivation\": null,\n  \"calendar\": null,\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": null,\n  \"annualized\": null,\n  \"entity_grain\": null,\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": null,\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"source\": \"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts API\",\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\",\n    \"retrieved_on\": \"2026-10-24\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Categorical label for the reporting window a fundamentals value covers. Values: Q (a single fiscal quarter), YTD6 (cumulative from fiscal year start through the second quarter), YTD9 (cumulative through the third quarter), FY (full fiscal year) and instant (a point-in-time balance, none in the sample rows). It is a grouping and filter key, not a measure, so it should not be aggregated. Rows with different bases for the same metric overlap (YTD9 includes Q1-Q3, and FY includes all quarters), so summing across period_basis values double-counts. Fiscal-year boundaries vary by company (e.g. WING starts around Dec 31 and DRI around late May), so period_start and period_end define the actual dates.\"\n}",
